UPDATE companies SET description='Island Pacific Distributors was founded on October 2, 1978, by Barbara and Leon Wolfley in Honolulu, Hawaii. The company began as a wholesale hardware and locksmith supply operation on King Street, serving the high-rise condominium boom in Waikiki and the Ala Wai corridor. In 2014, the business transitioned to an employee stock ownership plan (ESOP), making it fully employee-owned.

Today, IPD operates from a 35,000-square-foot facility in the Iwilei area of Oahu that includes offices, a warehouse, a showroom, and a steel door and frame fabrication shop. The shop is the only Warnock Hersey–marked facility in the state certified by Intertek to build and modify Assa Abloy’s Curries hollow metal doors and frames. The company distributes doors, frames, finish hardware, security products, and specialty building products, and also provides consultation, design, specification writing, installation, maintenance, electronic access control, and in-house locksmith services.

IPD serves architects, general contractors, and facility managers across Hawaii’s hospitality, commercial construction, government, and luxury residential sectors. Notable projects include the Allure Waikiki, Moana Surfrider, Sheraton Moana Surfrider, Four Seasons Resort Lanai, Disney Aulani Resort, Hokua, and the Kapolei Judiciary Complex. The company also lists medical, dental, and vision insurance among its served industries.', certifications=ARRAY['Warnock Hersey Mark (Intertek) for hollow metal doors and frames','Intertek Testing Services (ITS) / Warnock Hersey (WHI) file labeling','Certified Architectural Hardware Consultant']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Consultation & Analysis", "Design & Drawing (electronic)", "Specification & Technical Writing", "Installation (Expansion Joints, Overhead Coiling Doors/Grilles, Integrated Door Systems, Electronic Access Control Systems)", "Maintenance & Service", "Electronic Access Control (consultation, design, installation, tech support)", "In-House Locksmith (key cutting, rekeying, master keying)", "Steel Door Fabrication (hollow metal doors and frames, welding, modifications)", "Hollow Metal Door and Frame Fabrication (Warnock Hersey certified)", "Security Systems Design and Installation", "Specialty Building Products Distribution"], "industries": ["Hospitality", "Commercial Construction", "Government", "Luxury Residential", "Medical / Dental / Vision Insurance"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded October 2, 1978 by Barbara and Leon Wolfley -> /about", "Started as Wholesale Hardware and Locksmith Supply Company on King Street -> /about", "Employee-owned ESOP since 2014 -> /about", "35,000 sq ft facility in Iwilei with offices, warehouse, showroom, fabrication shop -> /about", "Only Warnock Hersey Mark shop in state certified by Intertek for Assa Abloy Curries hollow metal doors/frames -> /about", "Exclusive Hawaii distributor for Sargent Hardware -> /about", "Exclusive distributor for Total Door Openings System -> /about", "Exclusive Smoke Guard distributor and installer (2014) -> /about", "Added CornellCookson coiling and sectional doors (2016) -> /about", "Hawaii''s only certified Architectural Hardware Consultant -> /services", "In-house locksmith and steel door fabrication -> /services", "Services: Consultation & Analysis, Design & Drawing, Specification & Technical Writing, Installation, Maintenance & Service, Electronic Access Control -> /services", "Projects: Allure Waikiki, Moana Surfrider, Sheraton Moana Surfrider, Four Seasons Resort Lanai, Disney Aulani Resort, Hokua, Kapolei Judiciary Complex -> /", "Industries served: Medical / Dental / Vision Insurance -> db", "Serves architects, general contractors, management companies -> /about", "Staff averaging nearly 20 years tenure -> /about", "Motto ''Find A Way'' -> /about"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Island Pacific Distributors is the leading distributor of doors, frames, finish hardware, security products, and specialty building products in the Hawaiian islands.", "founded_year": "1978", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Employee-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='island-pacific-distributors' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='J & O Plastics operates from a 250,000-square-foot production and warehousing facility in Rittman, Ohio, located in the state''s retail distribution corridor. The company was founded in 1982 by Oscar and Christine Gross as an injection molding supplier to the Mr.

The company specializes in clear plastic injection molding, notably pioneering a proprietary process for straight PET that yields BPA-free, cosmetically clear parts at low cost. It also molds acrylic, polypropylene, SAN, crystal styrene, PVC, ABS, LDPE, and HDPE. Services encompass custom and large-part injection molding, in-line assembly, kitting, packaging, barcoding, SKU and inventory management, warehousing, and direct shipment to major retailers and Amazon FBA.

J & O serves household, industrial, agricultural, medical, and shipping/logistics markets.

The company differentiates itself through its early adoption of straight PET molding—one of few U.S. firms offering it—along with automation-driven competitive pricing, a lean facility that keeps scrap under 1 percent, and a commitment to same-day shipping and delivery from its centrally located Ohio plant.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Clear plastic injection molding", "Custom injection molding", "Precision injection molding", "PET injection molding", "Large part injection molding", "In-line assembly", "Assembly and kitting", "Packaging and labeling", "SKU and inventory management", "UPC barcoding", "Bulk packaging", "Warehousing", "Direct shipment to retail (Amazon FBA, Costco, Walmart, Target)", "Logistical support"], "industries": ["Household Products", "Industrial", "Agricultural", "Medical", "Shipping & Logistics", "Consumer Goods", "Retail", "OEM Industrial"], "materials": ["PET", "Acrylic", "Polypropylene", "SAN", "Crystal Styrene", "PVC", "ABS", "LDPE", "HDPE"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day shipping and delivery", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proprietary straight PET injection molding for BPA-free clear parts", "Certified direct shipping to Amazon FBA, Costco, Walmart, Target, and Bed Bath & Beyond", "In-line assembly, kitting, packaging, and inventory management under one roof", "Same-day shipping and delivery from a 250,000 sq ft Ohio facility", "Scrap rate maintained under 1% with full recycling program"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1982 by Oscar and Christine Gross -> /about-us", "Facility 250,000 sq ft in Rittman, Ohio -> /about-us", "Pioneered straight PET injection molding -> /about-us", "Certified to direct ship to Amazon FBA, Costco, Walmart, Target, Bed Bath & Beyond -> /about-us", "Materials: PET, Acrylic, Polypropylene, SAN, Crystal Styrene, PVC, ABS, LDPE, HDPE -> /", "Industries: Household, Industrial, Agricultural, Medical, Shipping & Logistics -> /", "Same-day shipping and delivery -> /about-us", "Scrap under 1% recycling -> /about-us", "In-line assembly, kitting, packaging, warehousing -> /about-us", "Headquarters Rittman, Ohio -> db", "Founded year 1982 -> db", "Company description: plastic injection molding solutions for shipping products and logistics -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "J&O Plastics has been a leader in the plastic injection molding industry since 1982.", "founded_year": "1982", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='j-o-plastics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Located in Westerly, Rhode Island, J & R Senior Sheetmetal, Inc. is a family-owned and operated business built on three generations of metalworking experience. The company traces its roots to over 40 years of roofing expertise and three decades of custom metal fabrication, though a specific founding year is not publicly disclosed.

The shop specializes in custom copper work, producing a range of architectural sheet metal components including roof vents, wall vents, drip edges, valleys, window and door pans, shower pans, step flashing, chimney caps, scuppers, and radius flashing. It also fabricates standing seam roof systems, flat-pounded panels, cupolas, chimney through-flashings, and radius roofs, with a dedicated line for .032 aluminum standing seam. In addition to fabrication, the company distributes Wuko tools and PREFA products and offers pre-packaged standing seam roof bundles that include high-temperature ice and water shield, wall flashings, drip edge, panels, clips, screws, Z-bar, and ridge caps. Production relies on a mix of antique hand tools and modern machinery, with an emphasis on quick turnaround.

The primary customers are builders, roofers, and homeowners throughout Rhode Island, including Block Island, with a focus on coastal construction that must withstand harsh New England weather. The company’s portfolio spans residential roofing, custom flashing, and specialty metal accents for both new builds and renovations.

J & R Senior Sheetmetal distinguishes itself through its multi-generational family ownership, deep roofing heritage, and a commitment to American-made products. The firm highlights its innovative approaches to coastal building challenges, personalized customer service, and the ability to deliver both standard and intricate custom pieces on short lead times.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom copper fabrication", "Roof vent flashing", "Roof exhaust vents", "Wall vents", "Drip edge fabrication", "Valley fabrication", "Window/door pan fabrication", "Shower pan fabrication", "Step flashing", "Drip cap fabrication", "Chimney cap fabrication", "Scupper fabrication", "Radius flashing", "Standing seam roof systems", "Flat-pounded roofing", "Cupola fabrication", "Chimney through-flashing", "Radius roof fabrication", ".032 aluminum standing seam fabrication", "Distribution of Wuko tools", "Distribution of PREFA products", "Standing seam roof bundle assembly"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Roofing", "Coastal construction", "Home building", "Renovation"], "materials": ["16oz copper", "Freedom Gray (Zinc Copper)", ".032 aluminum", ".032 painted aluminum"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated across three generations", "Over 40 years of roofing expertise", "Custom copper fabrication using antique hand tools and modern machines", "Quick turnaround times on custom and stock items", "Made in the USA"], "facts_used": ["Location: Westerly, Rhode Island -> db", "Family-owned and operated -> db, /", "Three generations of metalworking experience -> /", "Over 40 years of roofing expertise -> /", "Specializes in custom copper work -> db, /", "Products: roof vents, wall vents, drip edges, valleys, window/door pans, shower pans, step flashing, chimney caps, scuppers, radius flashing -> /", "Services: standing seam roof, flat-pounded, cupola, chimney through-flashing, radius roof, .032 aluminum standing seam -> /", "Distributor for Wuko tools and PREFA products -> /", "Standing seam roof bundles with components -> /", "Uses antique hand tools and modern machines -> /", "Quick turnaround times -> /", "Made in the USA -> /", "Serves builders, roofers, homeowners in Rhode Island including Block Island -> db, /", "Focus on coastal homes and harsh New England weather -> db, /", "Materials: 16oz copper, Freedom Gray, .032 aluminum, .032 painted aluminum -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "family-owned and operated business specializing in custom copper work", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='j-r-senior-sheetmetal-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='J.E. Fifer Sheet Metal Fabricators operates from a 30,000-square-foot facility in Richmond, Virginia. The company was founded in 1986 by James and Judy Fifer and remains family-owned, with their son Jason T. Fifer now serving as president.

The shop specializes in precision sheet metal fabrication, producing custom parts, assemblies, and complete machinery. Capabilities include CNC laser cutting, punching, and bending; TIG and MIG welding on aluminum, stainless steel, and mild steel; CNC PEM insertion; saw cutting; rolling; shearing up to 10 feet long and 1/4 inch thick in mild steel; and deburring on a Costa Metal Finishing machine. The facility also houses CNC and manual mills and lathes for precision machining, plus in-house shrink-packaging equipment that allows the company to deliver both fabricated components and proprietary packaging systems under one roof.

Fifer serves customers needing custom-built machinery, equipment upgrades, replacement parts, and shrink-packaging solutions. Its work supports industrial OEMs and manufacturers requiring fabricated metal components and integrated packaging equipment, though the company does not publicly list specific industry verticals.

The founders established the business on a commitment to quality products, timely communication, and on-time delivery — values that Jason Fifer says drive a mission of “ever-increasing satisfaction and sustainability through leadership, consistency, and integrity.” Repeat business is cited as the cornerstone of the company’s success.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC laser cutting", "CNC punching", "CNC bending", "Welding (TIG, MIG: aluminum, stainless steel, mild steel)", "CNC PEM insertion", "Saw cutting", "Rolling", "Shearing (10'' x 1/4\" mild steel)", "Deburring (Costa Metal Finishing machine)", "Precision machining (CNC & manual mills & lathes)", "Shrink packaging", "Custom machinery fabrication", "Equipment upgrades & replacement parts"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Aluminum", "Stainless Steel", "Mild Steel"], "equipment": ["Costa Metal Finishing deburring machine", "Shrink packing equipment", "CNC mills", "Manual mills", "CNC lathes", "Manual lathes", "Shearing machine (10'' capacity)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["30,000+ sq. ft. facility with in-house shrink-packaging equipment", "Family-owned since 1986 with second-generation leadership", "Core values: quality products, timely communication, on-time delivery", "Repeat business as cornerstone of success", "Single-source fabrication and packaging systems"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1986 -> /about", "Family-owned -> /about", "Founders James and Judy Fifer -> /about", "30,000+ sq ft facility -> /about", "Located in Richmond, VA -> /about", "Services: CNC Laser Cutting, CNC Punching, CNC Bending, Welding, CNC PEM Insertion, Saw Cutting, Rolling, Shearing, Deburring -> /", "Precision machining (CNC & manual mills & lathes) -> /", "Shrink packaging equipment in-house -> /about", "Custom-built machinery fabrication -> /", "Equipment upgrades & replacement parts -> /", "Welding on Aluminum, Stainless, Mild Steel -> /", "Deburring machine (Costa