UPDATE companies SET description='J Hunter Woodworks operates from Haddonfield, New Jersey, where founder Jeremy Hunter runs the shop as owner and master craftsman. The business grew from Hunter''s passion for design and building purposeful spaces that turn a house into a home, though the exact founding year is not publicly stated.

The company produces custom furniture and architectural woodwork, including built-ins, cabinets, dining tables, credenzas, bookshelves, breakfast nooks, and mantles. Every piece is hand crafted using high-quality, locally sourced wood. The Haddonfield location also offers an on-site experience where clients can build a custom dining table with handmade legs and tops. Output scale and headcount are not disclosed.

Clients include interior designers, individual homeowners, and corporate accounts. Testimonials reference projects such as a custom breakfast nook with storage drawers and upholstered cushions, a dining table with folding legs and stacking benches, and a mantle matched to existing flooring.

Hunter emphasizes a collaborative design process—"If you can dream it, I can build it"—and positions the workshop as an alternative to catalog or big-box furniture. The differentiators cited are the master-craftsman level of hand work, locally sourced materials, and the ability to involve customers directly in the design and on-site building experience.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture making", "Custom built-ins", "Cabinetry", "Dining table fabrication", "Breakfast nook construction", "Credenza making", "Bookshelf building", "Mantle fabrication", "Design consultation", "On-site custom table assembly"], "industries": ["Interior design", "Residential", "Corporate"], "materials": ["Wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Hand crafted by master craftsman Jeremy Hunter", "High-quality, locally sourced wood", "Collaborative custom design process", "On-site custom table building at Haddonfield showroom", "12 years of woodworking experience"], "facts_used": ["Location: Haddonfield, NJ -> db", "Founder: Jeremy Hunter -> /about", "Products: custom built-ins, cabinets, tables, credenzas, bookshelves -> /", "Process: hand crafted by master craftsman -> /", "Materials: high quality, locally sourced wood -> /", "Target customers: interior designers, individuals, corporate clients -> /", "Experience: 12 years woodworking experience -> /about", "On-site custom table building -> /", "Ownership: founder-owned -> /about", "Collaborative design process -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We create custom furniture, or built-ins for interior designers or individuals. The wood we use is high quality and locally sourced. Each piece is hand crafted by master-craftsman Jeremy Hunter.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='j-hunter-woodworks' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='JR Plastics & Machining, Inc. operates from Lowesville, Virginia, in the Blue Ridge Mountains about 25 miles south of Charlottesville. In 1998 the business added a full CNC machine shop, bringing mold making and secondary machining in-house.

The shop provides custom vacuum forming, hotwire bending, CNC machining, and engineering design services. Vacuum forming capacity reaches 24 by 50 by 9 inches deep in sheet up to 0.250 inch thick, using materials such as PETG, PVC, ABS, polycarbonate (Kydex), polystyrene, acrylic, and HDPE. CNC machining handles parts up to 50 by 100 by 9 inches in aluminum, brass, and stainless steel. Equipment includes HAAS mills, lathes, and routers, plus custom-built forming and bending machines maintained by the team.

Customers span medical, electronics, food packaging, and sports performance sectors, with the company noting satisfied clients across the United States. The firm emphasizes prototypes, short runs, and large-scale production, all managed under one roof.

The owners position the business on single-source convenience: clients work directly with Trent or Schneider from quote to delivery, and the in-house equipment fabrication allows rapid repairs to keep production on schedule.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom vacuum forming", "Hotwire bending", "CNC machining", "Engineering design services", "Pressure forming", "Jig and fixture design", "Custom mold making", "General machine work"], "industries": ["Medical", "Electronics", "Food packaging", "Sports performance"], "materials": ["PETG", "PVC", "ABS", "Polycarbonate (Kydex)", "Polystyrene", "Acrylic", "HDPE", "Aluminum", "Brass", "Stainless steel"], "equipment": ["HAAS mills", "HAAS lathes", "HAAS routers", "Custom-built forming equipment", "Custom-built bending equipment"], "volume": "Prototypes, small-run projects, and large-scale production runs", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Entire production process under one roof: vacuum forming, CNC machining, hotwire bending, and engineering", "Direct owner contact (David Trent or Raymond Schneider) from start to finish", "Custom-built forming and bending equipment for in-house repairs and minimal downtime", "Prototypes, small-run, and large-scale production runs", "Over 100 years of collective experience in vacuum forming, hotwire bending, and CNC machining"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1994 as custom vacuum forming firm -> /", "Added CNC machine shop in 1998 -> /", "Owners David Trent and Raymond Schneider -> /", "Location Lowesville, VA -> /", "Vacuum forming capacity 24x50x9 in, 0.250 in thick -> /", "Materials: PETG, PVC, ABS, Polycarbonate Kydex, Polystyrene, Acrylic, HDPE -> /", "CNC machining capacity 50x100x9 in, aluminum, brass, stainless steel -> /", "Equipment: HAAS mills, lathes, routers; custom forming/bending equipment -> /", "Industries served: medical, electronics, food packaging, sports performance -> /", "Services: engineering design, pressure forming, jig/fixture design, mold making -> /", "Collective experience over 100 years -> /", "Raymond Schneider 5+ decades experience -> /", "40 years machining/programming/jig fixture experience -> /", "Direct owner contact emphasized -> /", "In-house equipment repair capability -> /", "Prototypes, small-run, large-scale production -> /", "Company type: Manufacturer -> db", "Headquarters city/state from page -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Since 1994, JR Plastics & Machining, Inc. has provided custom vacuum forming for North America.", "founded_year": "1994", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='j-r-plastics-and-machining' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='J&L Plastic Molding operates from Wallingford, Connecticut, where it runs a molding facility across two buildings.

The shop specializes in injection molding, prototype and production tooling, insert molding, and tool transfer services. Its equipment lineup includes 28 injection molding machines with clamp forces from 28 to 385 tons and shot capacities of 0.6 to 24 ounces, enabling production of parts in engineering-grade thermoplastics such as PEEK, Ultem, Radel, and other high-performance resins.

J&L primarily serves medical device manufacturers, with LeMaitre Vascular recognized as a key customer—the company received LeMaitre''s Supplier of the Year award for quality, delivery, innovation, and collaboration. The firm''s ISO 13485:2016 certification supports its work in regulated medical applications.

The company emphasizes its ability to transition projects from development to production, maintain schedule-driven delivery, and process high-performance resins. Its tool transfer process allows customers to move existing tooling into J&L''s production system with minimal disruption.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection molding", "Prototype tooling", "Production tooling", "Insert molding", "Tool transfer", "Medical device molding", "Engineered resin processing"], "industries": ["Medical Device Manufacturing"], "materials": ["PPSU (Radel)", "PEI (Ultem)", "PEEK (Victrex)", "PPS (Ryton)", "LCP (Vectra)", "TPU", "TPE", "Polycarbonate", "ABS"], "equipment": ["28 injection molding machines (28\u2013385 ton clamp force, 0.6\u201324 oz shot size)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 13485:2016 certified for medical device manufacturing", "Tool transfer process for moving existing tooling into production", "28 injection molding machines (28\u2013385 ton clamp force)", "Engineering-grade material expertise (PEEK, Ultem, Radel, etc.)", "Supplier of the Year award from LeMaitre Vascular"], "facts_used": ["Company name and location -> db", "Facility: two buildings, 28 injection molding machines (28-385 tons, 0.6-24 oz) -> pages /", "Processes: injection molding, prototype tooling, production tooling, insert molding, tool transfer -> pages /", "Certification: ISO 13485:2016 certified by NQA -> pages /, db", "Industry: Medical Device manufacturers -> pages /, db", "Materials: PPSU, PEI, PEEK, PPS, LCP, TPU, TPE, Polycarbonate, ABS -> pages /", "Award: Supplier of the Year from LeMaitre Vascular -> pages /", "Headquarters address: 368 North Cherry Street Ext, Wallingford, CT 06492 -> pages /", "Website: http://www.jlmolding.com/ -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our Connecticut molding facility will supply all your production requirements and needs.