UPDATE companies SET description='J-Tech Construction and Solar was founded in 2004 in Lincoln, Nebraska.

The company provides residential and commercial roofing, metal siding, window and door installation, seamless gutter systems, and solar panel installation. J-Tech fabricates its own metal roofing and siding components in-house, allowing for custom fit and tighter quality control. The firm also uses drone technology for roof assessments. Its service area covers much of Nebraska, plus parts of Iowa, Kansas, South Dakota, and Missouri.

J-Tech serves residential homeowners and commercial property owners across its service territory. The company works with insurance restoration projects and offers financing for large exterior projects. Its customer base includes homeowners in Lincoln, Omaha, Grand Island, and surrounding communities, as well as commercial clients needing roofing, siding, or solar installations.

J-Tech differentiates itself through in-house metal fabrication, which ensures precise fit and quality control; drone roof inspections that provide clear documentation before work begins; and a single-contractor model that handles roofing, siding, windows, doors, gutters, and solar without subcontractors. The company highlights its 20-plus years in business, certifications as a ProVia Partner and James Hardie Contractor Alliance Partner, warranty-backed installations, and free inspections with no obligation.', certifications=ARRAY['ProVia Partner','James Hardie Contractor Alliance Partner','Nebraska Contractor Registration #36130-25']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Residential roofing", "Commercial roofing", "Metal roofing installation", "Storm damage restoration", "Emergency roof tarping", "Seamless steel siding installation", "Metal siding installation", "Door installation", "Window installation", "Seamless gutter system installation", "Residential solar panel installation", "Commercial solar panel installation", "In-house metal fabrication", "Drone roof inspections", "Insurance restoration"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Solar energy", "Roofing", "Exterior remodeling"], "materials": ["Asphalt shingles", "Metal", "James Hardie fiber cement", "Vinyl siding"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house metal fabrication for custom-fit components", "Drone roof inspections before any work begins", "Single-contractor model covering roofing, siding, windows, doors, gutters, and solar", "20+ years of continuous service in Nebraska", "ProVia Partner and James Hardie Contractor Alliance Partner certifications"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2004 -> db", "Headquarters in Lincoln, Nebraska -> db", "Roofing contractor for 20+ years -> /", "In-house metal fabrication -> /", "Drone roof inspections -> /", "Full exterior services (roofing, siding, windows, doors, gutters, solar) -> /", "Service area across Nebraska and parts of IA, KS, SD, MO -> /", "ProVia Partner through Window Depot USA -> /", "James Hardie Contractor Alliance Partner -> /", "Nebraska Contractor Registration #36130-25 -> /", "Materials: asphalt shingles, metal, James Hardie fiber cement, vinyl siding -> /", "Warranty-backed work -> /", "Free inspections and estimates -> /", "Financing available -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "J-Tech Construction & Solar has been Lincoln''s trusted roofing contractor for over 20 years. We handle roofing, metal siding, windows, doors, gutters, and solar \u2014 one team, one call, one contractor accountable from the first inspection to the final install.", "founded_year": "2004", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='j-tech-construction-and-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Operating from Minneapolis, Minnesota, J. Holtz Furniture is the workshop of woodworker J. Holtz. The business focuses on custom furniture and built-in cabinetry, with the owner personally guiding each project from concept to completion.

The shop produces one-of-a-kind furniture pieces, built-in cabinets, kitchen installations, doors, and architectural millwork, along with prototype work for other companies. Each order is built individually using hand-selected hardwoods, sourced locally when possible, and finished with a hand-rubbed finish. The process begins with a consultation, followed by sketches, scale drawings, and a quote before a deposit secures a place on the schedule.

Clients include homeowners seeking custom pieces, architects and designers specifying built-ins, and other manufacturers needing prototype development. The work draws on traditions such as Shaker, Scandinavian, Mid Century Modern, and Asian woodworking, reflecting a shared respect for craft and simplicity.

