UPDATE companies SET description='JB’s Tee Shirt Factory operates from New Berlin, Wisconsin, where it has served customers for over a decade. The business was founded by Jason Boesel, a UW‑Parkside graduate who brought 15 years of customer‑service experience and a background in product development and international business. Boesel remains the owner and president, overseeing a small team that includes production lead Berto Anguiano, a graphics graduate with more than 20 years in screen printing and three patent‑pending processes, and production assistant Zach Bartosiak, a MATC graduate focused on detail‑oriented registration and pressing.

The shop provides a full range of apparel decoration and manufacturing services: screen printing, embroidery, dye sublimation, heat transfers, and full cut‑and‑sew production. In‑house graphic design and template design support custom artwork, while contract printing services allow other businesses to outsource production. The company describes itself as a one‑stop source for workwear, team jerseys, and promotional items across Wisconsin.

