UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1926 in New York City, JMH Woodcraft Inc. has operated as a custom carpentry and cabinetmaking shop for nearly a century. The company serves the five boroughs from its Manhattan base, offering design, fabrication, and installation for residential and commercial projects.

The shop produces custom carpentry pieces including kitchen islands, built-in bookcases, radiator covers, wall units, and entertainment centers. As a small firm, JMH Woodcraft emphasizes personalized attention on projects of any scale, from single built-ins to full commercial fit-outs.

Clients range from homeowners to institutional and commercial accounts. Recent commercial projects include work for Mount Sinai School of Medicine, Christ and St. Stephens Church, V&T''s Restaurant, Firehouse Restaurant, Manhattan School for Children, Booker T. Washington Jr. High School, Beacon High School, and The Hungarian Pastry Shop. The company also serves residential customers throughout New York City.

