UPDATE companies SET description='JMW Fabrication, operating as JMW Specialty Welding and Fabrication, was founded in 2003 in Quakertown, Pennsylvania. The company provides mobile welding and in-house fabrication services from its shop in eastern Pennsylvania.

The shop runs CNC plasma cutting, press brake, iron worker, and automated cold saws, supporting processes such as SMAW, GMAW, and GTAW welding on steel, stainless steel, aluminum, cast iron, and cast steel. Capacity reaches thousands of pieces per day across small, medium, and large production runs, covering structural, architectural, stair, railing, repair, and prototype work.

Customers span residential, commercial, and industrial sectors throughout eastern Pennsylvania and New Jersey. Projects range from floating stairs and modern railings for homes to structural fabrication for commercial and industrial clients.

The company emphasizes long-term customer relationships over one-off jobs, with AWS‑certified welders (D1.1, D1.3, D9.1) and a mobile fleet that includes propane‑powered rigs for indoor welding. All major equipment is American‑made, and the firm prioritizes planning, communication, and craftsmanship quality.', certifications=ARRAY['AWS D1.1','AWS D1.3','AWS D9.1']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Mobile welding", "In-house fabrication", "CNC plasma cutting", "Press brake forming", "Punching and shearing", "Metal forming", "Automated cold saw cutting", "SMAW (Stick) welding", "GMAW (MIG) welding", "GTAW (TIG) welding", "Structural fabrication", "Architectural fabrication", "Stair fabrication", "Railing fabrication", "Repair services", "Production piece manufacturing", "Prototyping"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Industrial manufacturing", "Structural steel fabrication", "Architectural metalwork"], "materials": ["Steel", "Aluminum", "Stainless steel", "Cast iron", "Cast steel"], "equipment": ["CNC plasma table", "Press brake", "Iron worker", "Automatic cutting saws", "Mobile welding rigs (propane-powered)"], "volume": "Small to large production runs; thousands of pieces per day capacity", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["AWS\u2011certified welders (D1.1, D1.3, D9.1)", "Mobile welding rigs with propane power for indoor work", "In\u2011house CNC plasma table, press brake, iron worker, and automated cold saws", "All major equipment manufactured in the USA", "Business model focused on lasting customer relationships rather than single jobs"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2003 -> db", "Headquarters Quakertown, PA -> db", "Mobile welding and in-house fabrication -> /", "CNC plasma cutting, press brake, iron worker, automatic cutting saws -> /", "SMAW, GMAW, GTAW welding -> /", "Materials: steel, aluminum, stainless steel, cast iron, cast steel -> /", "Capacity thousands of pieces per day -> /", "Industries: residential, commercial, industrial -> /", "Service area: Eastern PA and New Jersey -> /", "AWS certifications D1.1, D1.3, D9.1 -> /", "Propane-powered mobile rigs for indoor welding -> /", "American-made equipment -> /", "Business model: acquire and serve good customers -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Mobile welding and in house welding repair and fabrication.", "founded_year": "2003", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='jmw-fabrication' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='JPM Steel Fabrication was founded in 2010 in Bella Vista, Arkansas, by James P. McGary, an Army veteran who served in Iraq from 2003 to 2005. After years working in concrete construction and storage-solution installation, McGary saw a shortage of skilled steel fabricators in the region and opened his own shop. The business is certified as a Veteran-Owned Small Business (VOSB) and is family-operated; McGary’s wife Erin, also an Army veteran, helps run the household while his brothers often lead installation crews.

The company designs, fabricates, and installs custom tension-fabric storage buildings—often called hoop sheds or fabric domes—for bulk materials such as grain, sand, salt, hay, and equipment. Beyond the fabric structures, JPM provides full-service maintenance, repair, retrofit (including “retrodomes” on existing foundations), cover replacement, and building relocation. The shop has grown from a single crew to multiple full-time steel fabricators, installation specialists, and office staff, and it also produces consumer items like steel benches and fire pits while performing general contracting for municipalities and large-scale commercial customizations.

JPM serves agriculture (farms, fisheries, grain storage), government and municipal agencies (salt and sand storage, maintenance buildings), waste and recycling facilities, aviation (aircraft hangars), mining operations, equestrian centers, port and intermodal terminals, and railroad depots. Customers range from individual farmers and construction companies to city, state, and federal agencies across the continental United States.

