UPDATE companies SET description='Jireh Semiconductor, Inc. operates as the dedicated wafer fabrication facility for Alpha and Omega Semiconductor (AOS) in Hillsboro, Oregon. Established as a wholly owned subsidiary of the NASDAQ-listed power semiconductor company (ticker: AOSL), the fab supports AOS’s vertical integration strategy. AOS itself was founded by Dr. Mike F. Chang, who serves as Chairman and Executive Vice President of Strategic Initiatives, and has been publicly traded since 2010.

The facility manufactures wafers for a broad portfolio of power semiconductors, including Power MOSFETs, IGBTs, intelligent power modules (IPMs), and power ICs. AOS emphasizes the integration of discrete and IC process technologies with advanced packaging know-how to deliver high-performance power management solutions.

The components produced at Jireh ultimately serve markets such as automotive (including EV powertrains), cloud and server infrastructure, telecommunications, computing (graphic cards, notebooks), consumer electronics, home appliances, industrial motor drives, power supplies, and power tools.

