UPDATE companies SET description='Kaempf & Harris Sheet Metal operates from Frederick, Maryland, as a division of the third-generation family-owned R.W. Warner, Inc. The Warner name dates to 1937, and Kaempf & Harris was founded in 1941. Matt Warner became CEO in 1998, continuing the family legacy.

The shop specializes in precision sheet metal fabrication, design-build services, broader metal fabrication, and on-site installation. Core processes include CNC laser cutting, press brake forming, turret punching, welding, riveting, and fastening, with finishing options such as painting, powder coating, and galvanizing. The facility produces more than 500 tons of metal annually, handling projects ranging from custom ductwork and pipe supports to structural brackets and frames. A notable project, Frederick’s Rose Hill Cancer Center, required over 75,000 pounds of fabricated sheet metal.

Its customer base includes mechanical contractors, general contractors, corporations, and institutions. Recent work includes the Hagerstown Multi-Use Sports Event Center, a $59.5 million downtown project, and ongoing support for mission-critical environments where system uptime and coordination are essential.

