UPDATE companies SET description='Keystone Electrical Manufacturing Company has operated from Des Moines, Iowa since its founding in 1964.

The company designs and produces power protection and control equipment, including custom control panels, substation control centers, power distribution centers, and medium-voltage switchgear. A vertically integrated facility handles sheet metal fabrication, assembly, wiring, and testing in-house. Engineering support, single-point project management, and detailed documentation — from panel layouts and schematics to as-built records — are provided alongside manufacturing.

Keystone serves electrical generation, transmission, and distribution utilities, as well as OEM partners in renewable energy such as wind turbine, transformer, and breaker manufacturers. Its low-voltage control panels are used in voltage regulation systems and industrial machinery. The company also assembles DC battery systems and installs utility services like HVAC, lighting, and security within control buildings.

Keystone emphasizes its vertically integrated workflow, dedicated project managers, and rigorous testing program. Every product undergoes in-process and final testing using a Doble F6150e test set, a Peschel 100 kV Hi-Pot, and a custom breaker simulator, with procedures aligned to IEEE/ANSI standards. Customers are invited to visit the facility for inspections and witness testing.', certifications=ARRAY['IEEE/ANSI standards (testing procedures)','UL 508A']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Engineering support services", "Sheet metal fabrication", "Electrical assembly and wiring", "In-process and final testing (Hi-Pot, functional, relay acceptance, high voltage, continuity, phase angle)", "Project management (single point of contact)", "Technical documentation (panel layouts, schematics, BOMs, as-builts, O&M manuals)", "Custom protection and control panel manufacturing", "Substation control center assembly (20''\u00d714'' to 60''\u00d730'' buildings)", "Power distribution center assembly (5\u201335 kV)", "Medium voltage switchgear assembly (2.4\u201338 kV)", "Low voltage control panel manufacturing (motor control, PLC, VFD, RTU/SCADA)", "Enclosure fabrication (indoor/outdoor, custom/off-the-shelf, various construction types)", "DC battery system installation (chargers, racks, spill containment, batteries)", "Utility system installation (HVAC, lighting, security, safety apparatus)", "Compliance testing per IEEE/ANSI, NEC, UL 508A"], "industries": ["Electrical power generation", "Electrical power transmission", "Electrical power distribution", "Utilities", "Renewable energy (wind turbine manufacturing)", "Transformer manufacturing", "Circuit breaker manufacturing", "Voltage regulation systems", "Industrial machinery", "OEM partners serving U.S. market"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Doble F6150e test set", "Peschel 100 kV Hi-Pot", "Custom breaker simulator"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated facility with in-house sheet metal fabrication, assembly, wiring, and testing", "Single-point project management with a dedicated manager for each contract", "Comprehensive as-built documentation tailored to customer specifications", "Rigorous testing using Doble F6150e, Peschel 100 kV Hi-Pot, and custom breaker simulator", "Open invitation for customer facility visits and witness testing"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1964 -> db (description)", "Headquarters in Des Moines, Iowa -> db (hq_city, hq_state_label)", "Manufactures power protection and control equipment -> page /", "Vertically integrated facility with sheet metal fabrication, assembly, wiring, testing -> page /", "Engineering support services and single-point project management -> page /", "Products: custom control panels, substation control centers, power distribution centers, medium voltage switchgear, low voltage control panels -> page /", "Industries: electrical generation, transmission, distribution; utilities; renewable energy OEMs (wind, transformer, breaker); voltage regulation; industrial machinery -> page /", "Equipment: Doble F6150e test set, Peschel 100 kV Hi-Pot, custom breaker simulator -> page /", "Testing per IEEE/ANSI standards, NEC, UL 508A compliance -> page /", "Customer facility visits for inspections welcomed -> page /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We manufacture products for the electrical generation, transmission, and distribution markets.", "founded_year": "1964", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='keystone-electrical-manufacturing-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ki USA Corporation has operated from Berea, Kentucky since its production start-up in August 1989. The company is a subsidiary of American Industrial Acquisition Corporation and began as a manufacturer of automotive engine, body, and suspension components.

The company specializes in precision metal stamping, robotic welding, and electro-deposition (e-coat) finishing, all housed in a 250,000-square-foot facility on 54 acres. The vertically integrated platform combines advanced metal stamping, programmable robotic welding systems, automated material handling, and an in-house e-coat line. The Berea site employs 160 associates, while a subsidiary in Irapuato, Guanajuato, Mexico, added in June 2015, employs 45 and provides localized support for Mexican customers.

Ki USA serves the automotive sector — including internal combustion, hybrid, and electric vehicle markets — with customers such as Honda, Mazda, and Ford. Its product portfolio includes engine mounts, brake boosters, engine oil pans, and other critical components. The company is also expanding into power generation and home appliance sectors.

Ki USA emphasizes trust, transparency, and community engagement as foundations of its culture. It cites its vertically integrated approach, extensive automation, and in-house e-coat process as differentiators that enable cost-competitive, high-quality solutions with faster turnaround. The company also highlights its commitment to continuous improvement, associate empowerment, and charitable initiatives such as Relay For Life and Soles4Souls.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Precision metal stamping", "Robotic welding", "Electro-deposition (e-coat) finishing", "Automated material handling", "Welded assemblies"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Power Generation", "Home Appliances"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Programmable robotic welding systems", "Automated material handling equipment", "In-house electro-coat (E-Coat) line"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated manufacturing: metal stamping, robotic welding, and e-coat finishing under one roof", "In-house electro-coat line for strict quality control and faster turnaround", "Extensive automation including programmable robotic welding systems and automated material handling", "Mexico subsidiary providing localized support and supply for customers in Mexico", "Commitment to trust, transparency, and continuous improvement culture"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1989, production start-up August 1989 -> /about", "Headquarters: Berea, Kentucky -> /about", "Parent company: American Industrial Acquisition Corporation -> /about", "Employees: 200+ (160 USA, 45 Mexico) -> / and /about", "Facility: 250,000 sq ft on 54 acres -> /about", "Processes: precision metal stamping, robotic welding, e-coat finishing -> /about and /", "Products: engine mounts, brake boosters, engine oil pans -> /about", "Customers: Honda, Mazda, Ford -> db", "Industries: automotive, power generation, home appliances -> / and /about", "Certification: IATF 16949:2016 -> /about", "Mexico subsidiary: Irapuato, Guanajuato, started June 2015 -> /about", "Automation: programmable robotic welding systems, automated material handling -> /about", "In-house e-coat line -> /", "Community involvement: Relay For Life, Soles4Souls -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Since 1989, KI (USA) has been a leading manufacturer of automotive engine, body, and suspension components in Berea, Kentucky.", "founded_year": "1989", "employee_count": "200+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ki-usa-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Kibberia Foods operates commercial kitchens in Danbury, Connecticut, and Lafayette, Louisiana. The company traces its roots to a restaurant opened in Danbury by founder Carole Iskandar and her husband Sam more than ten years ago, and it remains family owned and operated. In 2021, the business expanded to Lafayette to serve retailers in the Southeast.

The facilities produce more than 350 recipes and maintain an established line of over 250 SKUs, ranging from individual portions to food-service packaging. All ingredients are received and processed on the same day, and products are made fresh to order. The kitchens are certified under SQF, HACCP, and FSMA standards, with USDA inspection on site.

Kibberia Foods supplies large retailers and supermarkets, primarily in the Northeast and Southeast regions. Its customer base includes supermarket chains that carry the company''s all-natural, prepared foods under their own brands or the Kibberia label.

The company emphasizes a boutique approach to recipe development, offering rapid turnaround from concept to mass production in as little as one week. It also highlights flexibility in pricing, packaging, and seasonal adjustments, and donates surplus food to local charities.', certifications=ARRAY['HACCP','SQF','FSMA']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Recipe research and development", "Rapid new product development to mass production", "Trend analysis and menu planning", "Large-scale prepared food production (250+ SKUs)", "Boutique recipe creation approach", "Flexible packaging (individual, family, food service)", "Custom pricing and seasonal adjustment", "SQF and FSMA compliance", "HACCP plan implementation", "Annual performance audits", "USDA on-site inspection", "Same-day ingredient processing", "Fresh-to-order manufacturing", "Quality assurance and control", "Timely delivery and customer service"], "industries": ["Food retail", "Supermarkets", "Prepared foods"], "materials": ["Fresh ingredients", "All-natural ingredients"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "1 week for new product development to mass production", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["New product development to mass production in one week", "Same-day ingredient receiving and production", "SQF, HACCP, and FSMA certified facilities with USDA on site", "Family-owned and operated with a boutique recipe development approach", "Food surplus donated to local charities"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Lafayette, LA and Danbury, CT -> page /", "Family owned and operated -> page /", "Founder Carole Iskandar and husband Sam started as restaurant owners in Danbury over ten years ago -> page /", "Expanded to Lafayette, LA in 2021 -> page /", "Over 350 recipes and 250+ SKUs -> page /", "Same-day ingredient receiving and production -> page /", "Products made fresh to order -> page /", "SQF, HACCP, FSMA certifications; USDA on site -> page /", "Serves large retailers and supermarkets in Northeast and Southeast -> page /", "Rapid product development to mass production in one week -> page /", "Boutique approach to recipe development -> page /", "Flexible packaging and pricing -> page /", "Donates food surplus to local charities -> page /", "Certifications HACCP, SQF from database -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Kibberia Foods is a family owned and operated commercial kitchen, designed to provide high quality fresh foods to large retailers and supermarkets.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kibberia-fresh-foods' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Killdeer Mountain Manufacturing, Inc. was founded in 1987 in Killdeer, North Dakota.

The company produces cable assemblies, electrical wire harnesses, and fiber optic bundles for demanding applications. Its manufacturing capabilities encompass electrical wire harness assembly and fiber optic technology, including work to ARINC 807 aerospace standards.

KMM serves aerospace, military, and commercial aviation customers. Referenced programs include Boeing Wichita''s 767-GTTA, Lockheed Martin''s U-2, Seyers, and Southwest. The company holds terms agreements with Boeing Military, Boeing Commercial, and Lockheed Martin, indicating established supply relationships with major defense and aerospace primes.

KMM states that its cable assemblies incorporate first-rate materials to meet precise electrical, mechanical, and environmental requirements, and are designed for high-grade performance.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electrical wire harness assembly", "Cable assembly manufacturing", "Fiber optic bundle production", "Fiber optic technology (ARINC 807)"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Military/Defense", "Commercial aviation"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1987 -> db", "Headquarters Killdeer, ND -> db and homepage", "Additional offices Dickinson, Kerrville, Fargo, Bismarck -> homepage", "Makes cable assemblies, wire harnesses, fiber optic bundles -> homepage and db description", "Capabilities: electrical wire harness, fiber optics -> db capabilities and homepage", "Customers: Boeing Wichita 767-GTTA, Lockheed Martin U-2, Seyers, Southwest -> homepage", "Terms agreements with Boeing Military, Boeing Digital Product Definition, Lockheed Martin, Boeing, Purchase Order -> homepage", "First-rate materials for precise electrical, mechanical, environmental requirements -> homepage and db description", "Designed for high-grade performance -> homepage and db description", "ARINC 807 aerospace fiber optic standard -> db industries_served"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "KMM cable assemblies incorporate first-rate materials to meet precise electrical, mechanical and environmental requirements.", "founded_year": "1987", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='killdeer-mountain-manufacturing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Kindel Furniture Company traces its roots to 1886 when Albert F. Karges, a first-generation immigrant, invested $600 to begin making moderately priced American-style furniture from local hardwoods in Evansville, Indiana. Charles J. Kindel founded the Kindel Furniture Company in 1901. In 1964, John Fisher of Muncie, Indiana, purchased Kindel, and the Fisher family has maintained family ownership for over 50 years. The current entity, Kindel Grand Rapids, was formed when Kindel Furniture acquired the Karges and Councill Furniture companies, bringing together over 300 years of collective experience. The company is headquartered in Wyoming, Michigan, in the Grand Rapids area.

Kindel Grand Rapids produces made-to-order, handcrafted luxury furniture from its Grand Rapids facility. The product range spans dining, occasional, bedroom, and workspace categories, offered in styles including Timeless, Mid-Century Modern, Urban Modern, Transitional, Hollywood Glam, Organic, Coastal, Minimalist, Bohemian, and Industrial. Each piece is crafted to the precise specifications of the customer, emphasizing American craftsmanship and domestic production.

The company serves the luxury residential and commercial office furniture markets, working with interior designers and clients seeking signature, American-made pieces. Its workspace collections, marketed as defying office expectations, include desks, tables, credenzas, and components for traditional and transitional offices.

Kindel differentiates itself by championing a standard for domestic work while other companies have pursued lower-cost offshore production. The firm’s commitment to 100% American-made furniture and the preservation of a multi-generational craftsmanship heritage underpins its positioning.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Made-to-Order Furniture", "Handcrafted Furniture"], "industries": ["Luxury residential furniture", "Commercial office furniture", "Interior design trade"], "materials": ["Hardwoods"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% American-made furniture", "Family-owned since 1964 (Fisher family)", "Made-to-order handcrafted luxury", "Over 300 years of collective experience across Kindel, Karges, Councill", "Virtual 3D showroom tour"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1886 (Karges) -> /about", "Charles J. Kindel founded Kindel Furniture Company in 1901 -> /about", "Fisher family ownership since 1964 -> /about", "Headquarters in Grand Rapids, Michigan -> /about", "Wyoming, Michigan headquarters -> db", "Made-to-order handcrafted luxury furniture -> /about, /", "Styles: Timeless, Mid-Century Modern, etc. -> /", "Categories: Dining, Occasional, Bedroom, Workspace -> /", "Virtual 3D showroom tour -> /", "Acquired Karges and Councill -> /about", "Councill founded 1973 -> /about", "100% American-made commitment -> /about", "Over 300 years collective experience -> /about", "Family-owned business -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Kindel Grand Rapids creates made-to-order furniture that bears your signature style.", "founded_year": "1886", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kindel-furniture-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='King''s Wood Creation operates from a facility on West Rose Garden Lane in Phoenix, Arizona. The business traces its roots back more than twenty years to a one-person shop that gradually expanded into a full-scale woodworking operation.

The company produces a range of custom wood products including kitchen and bathroom cabinetry, fireplace mantels, ceiling box beams, furniture, hand railing, and architectural carvings. The facility also sources specialty wood species on request.

Its customer base spans building professionals such as contractors and designers as well as individual homeowners seeking bespoke cabinetry and millwork.

The firm emphasizes its ability to translate a client''s vision into a rendered design before fabrication begins, and it promotes a "dream it, we create it" philosophy backed by a ROC contractor license (#340054).', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cabinetry (kitchen, bath)", "Custom wood doors", "Fireplace mantels", "Ceiling box beams", "Custom furniture", "Hand railing", "Wood finishing", "Architectural carving", "CNC machining", "Design and rendering", "Specialty wood sourcing"], "industries": ["Building professionals", "Homeowners"], "materials": ["Wood", "Timber", "Specialty woods"], "equipment": ["CNC (Computerized Numerical Control) machinery"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Location: Phoenix, AZ -> db", "Founded over 20 years ago as one-person shop -> /", "Products: custom cabinets, doors, mantels, beams, furniture, railing, finishing, carvings -> /", "Processes: CNC machining, hand finishing -> /", "Customers: building professionals and homeowners -> /", "ROC license #340054 -> /", "Design and rendering service -> /", "Specialty wood sourcing -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "KWC has developed into one of the premier manufacturers of fine wood products in the USA.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='king-s-wood-creation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Kingsford Manufacturing Company operates from Parsons, West Virginia, where it has produced charcoal since 1920. The business emphasizes that its charcoal has been proudly made in the United States since its founding year. No founder names or ownership structure are disclosed in the available information.

The company manufactures a range of charcoal briquets and wood pellets for grilling. Product lines include Original, Professional, Mesquite, Match Light instant-light briquets, and the Easy Light Bag single-use format. Pellets are marketed as a premium-flavor option for pellet grills. The homepage does not provide facility size, headcount, or annual volume figures.

Kingsford’s products target consumer grilling occasions — tailgates, backyard barbecues, seafood cookouts, and everyday meals. No industrial or commercial customers are identified in the source material.

The company highlights its long-standing domestic production and flavor variety as differentiators. The Easy Light Bag is designed for fast, portable lighting, while the pellet line promises premium flavor without a premium price.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Charcoal briquet manufacturing", "Wood pellet manufacturing", "Flavor infusion (mesquite, etc.)", "Single-use bag packaging (Easy Light Bag)", "Instant-light briquet technology (Match Light)"], "industries": ["Consumer grilling", "Barbecue fuel", "Outdoor cooking", "Retail consumer goods"], "materials": ["Wood", "Mesquite wood", "Charcoal"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proudly made in the USA since 1920", "Variety of flavored charcoal briquets (Original, Professional, Mesquite)", "Match Light instant-light briquets that require no lighter fluid", "Easy Light Bag single-use format for portable grilling", "Wood pellets marketed as premium flavor without premium price"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1920 -> db", "Headquarters Parsons, West Virginia -> db", "Products: charcoal briquets (Original, Professional, Mesquite, Match Light, Easy Light Bag) and wood pellets -> page /", "Made in USA since 1920 -> page /", "Target consumer grilling occasions (tailgating, backyard, seafood) -> page /", "Differentiators: domestic production, flavor variety, easy light, premium pellets value -> page /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our charcoal has been proudly made in the USA since 1920.", "founded_year": "1920", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kingsford-manufacturing-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The business traces its roots to Clark’s early fascination with wood during a forestry program at the University of New Hampshire, followed by a carpentry apprenticeship under his uncle, master carpenter Robert Clark, in Montana. After studying at the Penland School of Crafts in North Carolina, Clark opened a studio in Bozeman, Montana, then relocated to North Ferrisburgh, Vermont in 2000. In 2007 he trained with chairwright Hal Taylor on Sam Maloof–style rocking chairs. The family moved to North Yarmouth in 2016, where Clark now runs the workshop as a solo maker.

The shop produces bespoke furniture ranging from rocking chairs and dining sets to beds, bookcases, and custom accessories. Each piece is handcrafted to order using a variety of domestic hardwoods; Clark works directly with clients to develop designs or adapt pieces from his gallery. There is no standardized production line—output is measured in individual heirloom items rather than volume batches.

Clients are primarily residential customers across the United States and Canada, including homeowners in North Carolina, Massachusetts, and as far as Singapore. The company ships finished pieces throughout the continental U.S. and Canada, and offers in-home consultations for local projects.

Clark cites a lifetime guarantee on every piece as a core differentiator, reflecting a commitment to durability. His design philosophy draws on the fluid forms of nature, and the Sam Maloof rocking-chair lineage informs the sculptural comfort of his seating. The business was built on the desire to create functional art that brings the peace of the outdoors into daily life.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design and fabrication", "Woodworking", "Rocking chair construction (Sam Maloof style)", "Furniture finishing", "In-home design consultation", "Shipping and delivery"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Custom woodworking"], "materials": ["Wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Lifetime guarantee on all furniture", "Ships anywhere in continental U.S. and Canada", "Custom designs from client concepts or gallery models", "Sam Maloof\u2013style rocking chair expertise", "In-home design consultation for local clients"], "facts_used": ["Location: North Yarmouth, Maine -> db", "Founder: Kit Clark -> /about", "Education: Associates Degree in Forestry, University of New Hampshire -> /about", "Apprenticeship under Robert Clark -> /about", "Penland School of Crafts attendance -> /about", "Studio in Bozeman, Montana -> /about", "Relocation to North Ferrisburgh, Vermont in 2000 -> /about", "Training with Hal Taylor in 2007 -> /about", "Move to North Yarmouth, Maine in 2016 -> /about", "Products: rocking chairs, chairs, dining sets, tables, beds, bookcases, custom accessories -> /services", "Lifetime guarantee -> /about, /services", "Shipping to continental US and Canada -> /about, /services", "In-home consultation for local clients -> /about, /services", "Custom designs from client ideas or gallery recreations -> /about, /services", "Sam Maloof style rocking chairs -> /about, /services", "Materials: variety of wood combinations -> /about", "Solo maker operation -> /about", "Clients in North Carolina, Singapore, Massachusetts -> /about", "Award winning furniture maker -> /", "Bespoke furniture -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "OFFERING A FULL LINE OF EXQUISITELY CRAFTED BESPOKE FURNITURE IN MAINE", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kit-clark-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Klingspor''s Woodworking Shop operates a retail location in Hickory, North Carolina, at 856 21st Street Drive SE. The business was founded in 1999 and serves as a specialty store for woodworking tools, supplies, and education.

The shop stocks a broad range of products including abrasives, router bits, saw blades, carving and turning tools, cabinet-making supplies, finishing products, hardware, power tools, dust-collection equipment, sharpening systems, safety gear, and both common and exotic lumber. It also carries CNC machines and accessories, such as Amana CNC bit sets. In addition to sales, the store runs in-store woodworking classes led by staff and guest instructors for all skill levels, and provides meeting space for several regional woodworking clubs.

Customers include hobbyists, professional woodworkers, woodturners, carvers, and pyrography artists. The Hickory store hosts monthly gatherings for the Southeastern Pyrography Association, the North Carolina Woodturners Association, the Catawba Valley Woodcarvers, and the Western Piedmont Woodcrafters, offering a venue for demonstrations, show-and-tell, and fellowship.

The company emphasizes hands-on learning and community, promoting its classes as a way for makers to build projects under expert guidance and its club partnerships as a hub for local woodworking culture. A weekly updated specials flyer and a newsletter called "Sawdust" keep customers informed on sales, classes, and club events.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Abrasives", "Woodworking tools", "CNC machines", "Wood blanks", "Wood turning finishes", "Finishing supplies", "Hardware and fasteners", "Safety products", "Common and exotic woods", "Woodworking classes", "Club meeting space"], "industries": ["Woodworking", "Woodturning", "Pyrography", "Woodcarving", "Cabinet making"], "materials": ["Wood (common and exotic)"], "equipment": ["CNC machines", "Amana CNC bit sets", "Dust collection machinery", "Sharpening stones"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-store woodworking classes for all skill levels", "Hosts multiple woodworking clubs and associations", "Weekly updated specials and promotions", "Carries common and exotic woods", "Offers CNC machines and Amana CNC bit sets"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1999 -> db", "Headquarters Hickory, NC -> db", "Capabilities: Abrasives, Woodworking Tools, CNC Machines, Wood Blanks, Wood Turning Finishes -> db", "Products: finishing supplies, hardware, safety products, woods, CNC machines, Amana CNC bit sets -> db", "Store address: 856 21st Street Drive SE, Hickory, NC 28602 -> /", "Store hours: Mon-Fri 8-6, Sat 9-5, Sun 1-5 -> /", "Offers woodworking classes for all skill levels -> /", "Hosts Southeastern Pyrography Association, NC Woodturners, Catawba Valley Woodcarvers, Western Piedmont Woodcrafters -> /", "Weekly specials and Sawdust newsletter -> /"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Products Available\nAbrasives (sandpaper, sanding discs, sanding belts, sanding pads)\nBits & Blades for routers, drills, band saws, table saws etc.\nBooks & DVD''s on all types of woodworking projects and plans\nCarving & Turning tools\nCabinet making tools, supplies, books and plans\nFinishing supplies, books and restore products\nHardware fasteners, hinges and screws\nPower Tools, Machinery, Dust Collection machinery, hoses and fittings, Sharpening stones, tools and machinery\nSafety products, Woods \u2013 common and exotic", "founded_year": "1999", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='klingspor-s-woodworking-shop' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Knectiv is based in Austin, Texas. The company was founded by Nicholas J. Frank, who serves as CEO, and Michael Lally, co-founder. Frank brought over a decade of experience in the Swiss electronics industry before establishing Knectiv to provide managed manufacturing services for complex hardware.

Knectiv provides end-to-end hardware commercialization, spanning product engineering, PCB manufacturing and assembly, plastic injection molding, conformal coating, press-fit and fine-pitch component placement (CSP, CCGA, BGA, 01005), systems integration, sourcing, and turnkey manufacturing. The firm coordinates global production with U.S.-side accountability and China-side execution, handling production planning, quality, packaging, and scale-up for clients.

The company serves industrial, medical, consumer, automotive, audio, and connected-hardware markets. Customers include GETS (Swiss medical-device manufacturer), Merging Technologies Switzerland, Zefon International (air-quality measurement systems), and CEBI Micromotors Switzerland (automotive sub-assemblies). Portfolio projects range from microhematocrit centrifuges and LFIA readers to endoscopic insufflators, blood-pressure monitors, and Bluetooth-enabled pedals.

Knectiv emphasizes a unified approach: a single point of contact, consistent quality across the manufacturing chain, and efficiency gains by consolidating multiple vendors. Its stated mission centers on sustainability, innovation, integrity, collaboration, and excellence, aiming to make hardware development easier while delivering positive societal and environmental impact.', certifications=ARRAY['ROHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Product engineering", "Design for manufacturing (DFM)", "PCB manufacturing", "PCB assembly", "Plastic injection molding", "Conformal coating", "Press-fit assembly", "CSP/CCGA/BGA/01005 placement", "SPI molding finishes", "Systems integration", "Production planning", "Quality management", "Assembly and packaging", "Scale-up support", "Component sourcing", "Turnkey manufacturing", "Global manufacturing coordination", "Cost and production review", "Firmware coordination", "Test fixture design", "Enclosure design", "Mechanical design"], "industries": ["industrial", "medical", "consumer", "automotive", "audio", "connected hardware"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Automatic Conformal Coating System"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["One accountable path from product engineering to manufacturing execution", "US-side accountability with global manufacturing coordination (China-side execution)", "Simplified management through a singular point of contact", "Consistent quality standards across all manufacturing steps", "Efficiency by eliminating the complexity of managing multiple suppliers"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Austin, Texas -> db", "Founders: Nicholas J. Frank (CEO), Michael Lally (Co-Founder) -> /about-us", "Frank''s background: over a decade in Swiss electronics industry -> /about-us (testimonial)", "Services: product engineering, PCB manufacturing/assembly, plastic injection molding, conformal coating, press-fit, fine-pitch placement, systems integration, sourcing, turnkey manufacturing -> /"