UPDATE companies SET description='Kulite Semiconductor Products was founded in 1959 by Dr. Anthony D. Kurtz in Leonia, New Jersey, where the company maintains a three-building, 200,000-square-foot campus. A physicist with degrees from MIT, Dr. Kurtz had previously worked at Honeywell before returning to New Jersey to start the business. The family-founded, woman-owned enterprise is now led by his widow, Nora Kurtz, who assumed leadership after his death in 2010.

The company designs and manufactures pressure transducers and sensors for extreme environments, offering pressure ranges from 1 to 60,000 PSI, operating temperatures from -320°F to 932°F, and resistance to vibration up to 100g. Its product line includes unamplified and amplified outputs, submersible transmitters, pressure switches, and redundant sensor configurations. Kulite holds over 400 patents and produces both standard catalog items and thousands of custom designs.

Kulite serves aerospace and defense, automotive (including Formula One and IndyCar testing), marine, space, and process-control industries. Its transducers are used on commercial aircraft such as the Boeing 747, naval vessels, oil-exploration equipment, and weather balloons. The company describes itself as the world''s largest supplier of aerospace transducers.

Dr. Kurtz established the company to become the worldwide expert in transducer technology, emphasizing long-term employee retention, university partnerships, and continuous R&D investment. The firm cites its patent portfolio, custom-engineering capability, and woman-owned, family-led structure as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Pressure sensors (absolute, gage, sealed gage, differential)", "High proof pressure (5 to 200 times overload)", "Pressure ranges 1 PSI to 60,000 PSI full scale", "Temperature extremes: -320\u00b0F to 932\u00b0F continuous operation", "Simultaneous static and dynamic pressure measurements", "Bridge resistance 1,000 ohms typical (350 to 15,000 ohms custom)", "High vibration resistance (100g peak, sine 10-5,000 Hz)", "Shunt calibration option", "Transducer outputs: unamplified (30-300mV), amplified (0-5V, 0.5-5V, 0-10V, 4-20mA), special amplified (potentiometer/LVDT/variable reluctance replacement)", "Custom sensor physical shapes and configurations", "Submersible transducers/transmitters to 1,100 ft depth", "Pressure switches with single or multiple switched outputs", "Dual and triple redundant sensor designs", "Gage pressure measurements within hermetically sealed transducer"], "industries": ["Aerospace / Defense", "Automotive", "Automotive Test / Motorsport", "Marine", "Space", "Process Control", "Oil & Gas", "Mining", "Meteorology"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 400 patents in transducer technology", "World''s largest supplier of aerospace transducers", "Family-founded, woman-owned business with 200,000 sq ft R&D and manufacturing campus", "Custom and stock pressure transducers for extreme environments (-320\u00b0F to 932\u00b0F, up to 60,000 PSI)", "Collaborating with customers since 1959 to create thousands of custom designs"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1959 by Dr. Anthony D. Kurtz -> /about", "Headquarters in Leonia, NJ with 200,000 sq ft campus -> /about", "Woman-owned, family-founded -> /about", "Over 400 patents -> /about", "World''s largest supplier of aerospace transducers -> /about", "Pressure ranges 1-60,000 PSI -> /capabilities", "Temperature extremes -320\u00b0F to 932\u00b0F -> /capabilities", "Industries: aerospace/defense, automotive, marine, space, process control -> /about and /", "Custom transducer designs for Formula One and IndyCar -> /about", "Employee count over 800 at peak -> /about", "Dr. Kurtz PhD from MIT, worked at Honeywell -> /about", "Nora Kurtz leads company since 2010 -> /about", "Submersible transducers to 1,100 ft -> /capabilities", "Redundant sensor designs -> /capabilities", "Pressure switches -> /capabilities", "Bridge resistance options -> /capabilities", "High vibration resistance 100g -> /capabilities", "Simultaneous static/dynamic pressure measurement -> /capabilities", "Shunt calibration option -> /capabilities", "Transducer output options -> /capabilities", "Custom sensor shapes -> /capabilities", "Federal defense contract requirements (export license restrictions) -> /quality", "Equal opportunity employer -> /quality", "Knowledge of FAR preferred -> /quality"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "As the premier supplier, designer and manufacturer of both commercial and military aircraft applications, Kulite single-handedly revolutionized the pressure transducer for the aerospace industry.", "founded_year": "1959", "employee_count": "over 800", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned", "Woman-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kulite-semiconductor-products' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Kyana Packaging Solutions traces its roots to 1976, when Dave and Inez White launched Kyana Industrial Supply from their home in Louisville, Kentucky. Dave White left his previous job convinced he could deliver greater value to customers than the market offered, and the couple built the business around that principle. Now operating as Kyana Packaging Solutions, the company remains headquartered in Louisville.

The company operates across three divisions. Kyana Packaging Solutions distributes a broad line of packaging supplies — corrugated boxes, tapes, poly bags, stretch and shrink films, cushioning, cold-chain materials, labels, strapping, safety and janitorial products — and sells packaging equipment. ASR Solutions provides third-party logistics, kitting, and assembly services, turning components into ready-to-ship kits. Bethlehem Die Cutting produces custom die-cut parts for specialized packaging and industrial applications. The firm also offers a packaging assessment program to help clients optimize their packaging spend and performance.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Packaging supplies distribution", "Custom corrugated packaging design and manufacturing", "Third-party logistics and warehousing", "Kitting and assembly", "Custom die-cutting", "Packaging assessment and consulting", "Packaging equipment sales and service", "Cold chain packaging solutions", "Strapping and banding systems", "Void fill and cushioning systems", "Labeling solutions", "Safety and janitorial supply distribution"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom corrugated packaging design and manufacturing", "Third-party logistics and fulfillment through ASR Solutions", "Kitting and assembly services", "Custom die-cut components via Bethlehem Die Cutting", "Packaging assessment program"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1976 by Dave and Inez White in Louisville, Kentucky -> db", "Operates three divisions: Kyana Packaging Solutions, ASR Solutions, Bethlehem Die Cutting -> page:/", "Distributes packaging supplies including corrugated boxes, tapes, poly bags, stretch film, cushioning, labels, strapping, safety products -> page:/", "Provides third-party logistics, kitting, and assembly via ASR Solutions -> page:/", "Produces custom die-cut components via Bethlehem Die Cutting -> page:/", "Offers packaging assessment program -> page:/"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Kyana Packaging Solutions was founded in 1976 as Kyana Industrial Supply by Dave and Inez White in their home.", "founded_year": "1976", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kyana-packaging-solutions' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
